<div class="html" id="tag">
<article class="env-proposition" id="0340">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0340">Proposition <span data-tag="0340">4.5.5.4</span>.</a> A commutative diagram of simplicial sets </p>
<div class="equation" id="0341">
<span class="equation-label"><a data-tag="0341" href="/tag/0341">4.33</a></span>
<div>\begin{equation}  \begin{gathered}\label{equation:categorical-pushout-to-categorical-pullback} \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ A \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  A_0 \ar [d] \\ A_1 \ar [r] &amp;  A_{01} } \end{gathered} \end{equation}</div>
</div>
<p> is a categorical pushout square if and only if it satisfies the following condition: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(\ast )$</dt>
<dd><p>
For every $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, the diagram of $\infty $-categories 
</p>
<div class="equation" id="0342">
<span class="equation-label"><a data-tag="0342" href="/tag/0342">4.34</a></span>
<div>\begin{equation}  \begin{gathered}\label{equation:categorical-pushout-to-categorical-pullback2} \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{Fun}(A,\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) &amp;  \operatorname{Fun}( A_0, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \ar [l] \\ \operatorname{Fun}(A_1, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \ar [u] &amp;  \operatorname{Fun}( A_{01}, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \ar [l] \ar [u] } \end{gathered} \end{equation}</div>
</div>
<p>
 is a categorical pullback square. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Fix an $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. If the diagram of $\infty $-categories (<a data-tag="0342" href="/tag/0342">4.34</a>) is a categorical pullback square, then the diagram of cores 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{Fun}(A,\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})^{\simeq } &amp;  \operatorname{Fun}( A_0, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}})^{\simeq } \ar [l] \\ \operatorname{Fun}(A_1, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}})^{\simeq } \ar [u] &amp;  \operatorname{Fun}( A_{01}, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}})^{\simeq } \ar [l] \ar [u] } \]
</div>
<p>
       is a homotopy pullback square (Proposition <a data-tag="033C" href="/tag/033C">4.5.3.15</a>). Allowing $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ to vary, we see that if $(\ast )$ is satisfied, then (<a data-tag="0341" href="/tag/0341">4.33</a>) is a categorical pushout square. For the converse, assume that (<a data-tag="0341" href="/tag/0341">4.33</a>) is a categorical pushout square. For every simplicial set $X$, the simplicial set $\operatorname{Fun}(X, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$ is an $\infty $-category (Theorem <a data-tag="0066" href="/tag/0066">1.5.3.7</a>), so the diagram of Kan complexes 
    <p>
<div class="equation" id="0343">
<span class="equation-label"><a data-tag="0343" href="/tag/0343">4.35</a></span>
<div>\begin{equation}  \begin{gathered}\label{equation:categorical-pushout-to-categorical-pullback25} \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{Fun}( A, \operatorname{Fun}(X, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}))^{\simeq } &amp;  \operatorname{Fun}(A_0, \operatorname{Fun}(X, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) )^{\simeq } \ar [l] \\ \operatorname{Fun}(A_1,\operatorname{Fun}( X, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}))^{\simeq } \ar [u] &amp;  \operatorname{Fun}(A_{01}, \operatorname{Fun}(X, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}))^{\simeq } \ar [u] \ar [l] } \end{gathered} \end{equation}</div>
</div>
<p>
       is a homotopy pullback square. Identifying (<a data-tag="0343" href="/tag/0343">4.35</a>) with the diagram 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{Fun}( X, \operatorname{Fun}(A, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}))^{\simeq } &amp;  \operatorname{Fun}(X, \operatorname{Fun}(A_0, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) )^{\simeq } \ar [l] \\ \operatorname{Fun}(X,\operatorname{Fun}( A_1, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}))^{\simeq } \ar [u] &amp;  \operatorname{Fun}(X, \operatorname{Fun}(A_{01}, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}))^{\simeq } \ar [u] \ar [l] } \]
</div>
<p>
       and allowing $X$ to vary, we conclude that the diagram (<a data-tag="0342" href="/tag/0342">4.34</a>) is a categorical pullback square (Proposition <a data-tag="033C" href="/tag/033C">4.5.3.15</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
